<title>USA: Franklin Select Realty Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Franklin Select Realty Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SAN MATEO, Calif. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>FRANKLIN SELECT REALTY TRUST</p>
<p>			    SELECTED FINANCIAL DATA</p>
<p>	    (Amounts in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>						 Restated  Restated</p>
<p>				   9/30/96  9/30/95  9/30/96  9/30/95</p>
<p>REVENUES:</p>
<p> Rental Income			$3,412 $3,408 $10,144 $10,087</p>
<p> Interest and Dividends		185    189     540     531</p>
<p>     Total revenue		   3,597  3,597  10,684  10,618</p>
<p>EXPENSES:</p>
<p> Interest				  153    187     467     509</p>
<p> Operating expenses		  1,006  1,127   2,690   2,811</p>
<p> Depreciation and amortization     836    833   2,491   2,507</p>
<p> Related party expenses		304    260     864     772</p>
<p>General and administrative</p>
<p>   expenses				137    124     474     356</p>
<p> Consolidation expense, net	 (26)    173     680     173</p>
<p>    Total expenses		   2,410  2,704   7,666   7,128</p>
<p> Net income			    1,187    893   3,018   3,490</p>
<p>Net income per share of</p>
<p>   Series A common stock	     .08    .06     .21     .25</p>
<p>Dividends per share of Series</p>
<p>   A common stock			.11    .11     .33     .33</p>
<p> Funds From Operations	     2,023  1,726   5,509   5,997</p>
<p> Per share				 .14    .12     .39     .42</p>
<p>Funds From Operations</p>
<p>   excluding merger expenses     1,999  1,919   6,263   6,190</p>
<p> Per share				 .14    .14     .44     .44</p>
<p>On Nov. 1, 1996, the Company purchased all of the outstanding dissenting shares of common stock related to the merger of the Company with two other real estate investment trusts in May 1996. The dissenting shareholder agreed to sell its 634,137 dissenting shares of Series A common stock in the Franklin Real Estate Income Fund and 1,077,608 dissenting shares of Series A common stock in the Franklin Select Realty Trust for a total price of $8.4 million. After giving effect to the transaction, the total number of Series A common stock outstanding for purposes of calculating net income per share and cash distributions per share will decline to approximately 12.25 million shares.</p>
